# .dockerignore — what enters the Docker build context.
#
# Docker does NOT read .gitignore. Without this file the context is "everything
# in the directory", which on a developer's machine includes untracked work.
#
# That is not hypothetical: the first build of the baked-addons image picked up
# twelve modules from a working tree where only seven were tracked — silently
# baking the entire unreleased WhatsApp suite into what would have been a
# production image.
#
# Cloud Build gets a clean git checkout and would not have had that problem,
# which is worse, not better: local and CI builds would disagree, and only the
# local one would be wrong. Keeping both honest is the point of this file.
#
# The pipeline additionally ASSERTS that the baked module list matches the
# git-tracked list, so a gap here fails CI rather than reaching production.

.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gcloudignore

# Vendored upstream Odoo — provided by the FROM odoo:19.0 base image.
addons/
odoo/
doc/
debian/
setup/
odoo-bin

# Runtime data that must never enter an image.
odoo-db-data/
odoo-web-data/
letsencrypt/
.env

# Editor and OS noise. .DS_Store was baked into the first build.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Infrastructure and docs are not application code.
infrastructure/
docs/
postman/
*.md
docker-compose.yml
**/terraform.tfvars
